\DOC CONTAINED_ASM_TAC

\TYPE {CONTAINED_ASM_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a goal asserting that one address range is contained, modulo a power of
two, within another, by arithmetic reasoning from the goal's assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion {t} is a
containment-modulo statement between two (base, length) pairs, it closes the
goal:
{
   A ?- t
   =============  CONTAINED_ASM_TAC
      (no goals)
}
\noindent Since nothing remains, the assumption list is untouched.

\FAILURE
Fails when the containment in the conclusion does not follow by linear
arithmetic from the available numeric assumptions: the internal arithmetic
decision step finds no contradiction and raises a failure. In the observed
traces this occurs for conclusions relating ranges whose relative placement the
assumptions do not constrain, including ones whose length involves a non-linear
operator.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of success, always on goals of that
single conclusion form carrying a large assumption list of machine-state, size
and bound facts.

\ENDDOC
